      "text": "Signal Processing - Neural Data (Jupyter notebook, 2026).\nSignal Processing - Neural Data is a solo Jupyter notebook for a brain signal processing course, in Python with NumPy and SciPy, that smooths a voltage-imaging recording and analyzes spike trains. Part 1 covers sampling, the Nyquist rate, aliasing and quantization. Part 2 smooths a voltage-sensitive-dye recording from a leech ganglion with rectangular and triangular filters and measures SNR. Part 3 analyzes synthetic spike trains from five neurons: firing rates, Fano factor, inter-spike intervals, PSTHs, and auto- and cross-correlation.\nTech: Python, NumPy, SciPy, Pandas, Matplotlib, Jupyter.\nCode: https://github.com/Royc4515/Project1_SignalProcessing\nGitHub repo Project1_SignalProcessing: Jupyter Notebook, last push 2026-05-17.",
